  J  Leung  MD  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by OH KIRSTINE YUNG TING M D   The specimen is received fresh in one part   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name   unit number and  left breast mass inking per pathology protocol   Attached  with the specimen is a mammogram demonstrating a fragment of breast tissue with  a wire localizing needle in the specimen  a small density  and very faint  calcifications  The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm and is received inked  per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black   anterior   blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial    orange  Serial sectioning reveals yellow tan fatty tissue throughout the  specimen  No focal lesions or fibrous tissue is identified  The specimen is  entirely submitted from medial to lateral   Micro 1  medial border of breast tissue  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections of breast tissue  1 frag each  ESS  Micro 11  lateral border of breast tissue  2 frags  ESS  ko  Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , Absent.
