ENCE OF MALIGNANCY   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen s  were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN INFERIOR  EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIPLE FOCI PRESENT IN 2 OF 2 TISSUE BLOCKS  EXTENDING TO  0 1 CM FROM THE MARGIN DESIGNATED BY A SUTURE IN SEVERAL FOCI  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior  a long stitch designating medial  and needle localization wire in place  The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph  The specimen is inked according to protocol  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  inferior   yellow and serially sectioned from medial to lateral  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular cavity which may represent a previous biopsy site which extends to within 0 3cm of the superior  0 6cm of the posterior and anterior  2 0cm of the inferior  0 9cm of the medial  0 3cm of the lateral margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a moderate amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  Identified adjacent to the previous biopsy site is a metallic clip  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Body of specimen submitted sequentially from medial to lateral  with the section which contains the clip in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end en face  Received are five containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Rece